Chapter: BlockLadderProbe
  cites Works chapter MetalLadder

 What A5 could not answer on 2026-08-10: the compiler payload reached the
 board, painted nothing of its own, wrote nothing, and the volume came back
 byte-identical. Every stage between entry and the write was collapsed into
 one silent state. This walks those stages and paints each one.

 THE PAINT MUST PRECEDE THE PRINT ON EVERY RUNG, and the first version of
 this chapter got that backwards. print-line-uni reaches firmware ConOut,
 and the kernel loads its own CR3 before any of this runs (X86_64Boot, the
 uefi-systab-addr note), so a firmware call here is a jump into a mapping we
 replaced. On the ASUS, 2026-08-10, the payload produced no colour and no
 write and the screen held the stub's dark green: a print that never returns
 explains that exactly, and with the print first the colour channel could not
 run to say so. Ordering the paint first makes the colour independent of
 ConOut, which is what having two channels was supposed to buy.

 fb=1 on a stage line means the colour was read back out of the framebuffer
 after it was written, so a silent paint convicts itself.

 We say:

Section: Cells

 uefi-systab-addr, the cell cdx-to-pe.ps1 primes with the SystemTable
 pointer before it jumps. It moved to 30704 at main 14398 because 36208 sat
 inside the PML4 the page-table build zeroes.

  probe-systab-cell : Integer = 30704

 The ESP as build-img.ps1 lays it out. flash-usb.ps1 -SpecFit rewrites LBA 0
 and 1 and the backup GPT, and moves neither the partition nor its BPB.

  probe-part-lba : Integer = 2048

 Inside the facts region (LBA 28639..32734 on a 32768-sector image), so a
 test write lands on nothing the volume's own checks read.

  probe-scratch-lba : Integer = 30000

  probe-mark-a : Integer = 165

Section: Entry

  probe-bps : Integer -> Integer
  probe-bps (buf) = peek-byte buf 11 + bit-shl (peek-byte buf 12) 8

 The read rung tests the CONTENT, not the pointer. Testing buf /= 0 tests
 that a buffer was allocated, which is true whether or not any sector
 arrived in it: a payload built without UEFI mode reads down the bare-metal
 path, gets 512 zero bytes, and passes a pointer test every time. The
 0x55AA signature at 510 is in every boot sector build-img.ps1 lays down.

  probe-read-ok : Integer -> Integer
  probe-read-ok (buf) =
    if buf == 0 then 0
    else if peek-byte buf 510 /= 85 then 0
    else if peek-byte buf 511 /= 170 then 0
    else 1

  probe-truth : Boolean -> Integer
  probe-truth (b) = if b then 1 else 0

  probe-step : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  probe-step (tag) (ok) (colour) (prev) = act
    fb <- ladder-pass ok colour prev
    print-line-uni ("LADDER " & tag & " ok=" & show ok & " painted fb=" & show fb)
    h <- ladder-hold-if ok prev
    print-line-uni ("LADDER " & tag & " continuing")
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Integer = act
    a <- probe-step "entered" 1 ladder-cyan ladder-red
    print-line-uni ("LADDER fb base=" & show (boot-fb-base 0) & " w=" & show (boot-fb-w 0) & " h=" & show (boot-fb-h 0) & " stride=" & show (boot-fb-stride 0))
    b <- probe-step "systab" (probe-truth (peek-qword probe-systab-cell 0 /= 0)) ladder-yellow ladder-cyan
    sb <- block-read-sector probe-part-lba
    c <- probe-step "read" (probe-read-ok sb) ladder-magenta ladder-yellow
    print-line-uni ("LADDER bps=" & show (probe-bps sb) & " b0=" & show (peek-byte sb 0) & " b11=" & show (peek-byte sb 11) & " b12=" & show (peek-byte sb 12))
    d <- probe-step "bpb" (probe-truth (probe-bps sb == 512)) ladder-orange ladder-magenta
    m0 <- poke-byte sb 0 probe-mark-a
    wr <- block-write-sector probe-scratch-lba sb
    rb <- block-read-sector probe-scratch-lba
    e <- probe-step "readback" (probe-read-ok rb) ladder-orange ladder-magenta
    f <- probe-step "wrote" (probe-truth (peek-byte rb 0 == probe-mark-a)) ladder-white ladder-orange
    ladder-hold ladder-white
  end
